<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Alkalawa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1808</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulani-war">Fulani War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alkalawa">Alkalawa</a> was the capture in 1808 of Alkalawa, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobir">Gobir</a>, by the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a>. The Gobir ruler was killed. The victory destroyed the main Hausa opponent of the jihad and was a decisive step in the establishment of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
